"engenn5le14ob06re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Past Tense and Past Continuous Tense", "type": "heading"}, {"content": "You use the Simple Past tense to talk about events that are finished. You use the Past Continuous to talk about events or an action that was happening at a time in the past.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ann</span>: Did you bump your head in the accident? </br><span class=\"strong\">Bob</span>: No. I was wearing my seatbelt when it happened.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "For Simple Past, regular verbs end in <span class=\"strong\">-ed</span> or <span class=\"strong\">-ied</span>.</p> Irregular verbs change in different ways.</p> For Past Continuous, we add <span class=\"strong\">was/were</span> + verb\u201c<span class=\"strong\">ing</span>\u201d to verbs.</p> You use Past Continuous verbs to describe a longer action that is interrupted by a shorter action.</p> You use Simple Past verbs to describe the shorter action.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "{\"rows\":8,\"columns\":3,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Present\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Past Continuous\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"brake\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"braked\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were braking\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bump\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"bumped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were bumping\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wear\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"wore\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were wearing\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"run\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"ran\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were running\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"step\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"stepped\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were stepping\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"drive\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"drove\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were driving\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"think\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"thought\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"was/were thinking\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}", "type": "table"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to run someone over ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to knock someone down with a vehicle", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We almost ran someone over on our way to the pyramids!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob06aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": "These are words you use when you talk about injuries and accidents.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to sprain", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to twist and injure a joint in your body", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I stepped into a hole and sprained my ankle", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob06aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "ankle", "type": "name"}, {"content": "the part of the foot that connects to the leg", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: When you hurt your ankle, it is difficult to walk.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob06aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "whiplash", "type": "name"}, {"content": "an injury caused by a sudden jerk to the head, typically in a car accident", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I didn't bump my head, but I had whiplash for a few days.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob06aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "injured", "type": "name"}, {"content": "harmed; suffering from an injury", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: We had an accident but no one got injured.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob06aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "seriously", "type": "name"}, {"content": "badly; not lightly", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adverb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Was anyone seriously injured?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob06aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "life-threatening", "type": "name"}, {"content": "serious with the possibility of death as an outcome", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(adjective)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Fortunately for Andrew, his injuries weren't life-threatening!", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn5le14ob06aud07", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Think about an event that happened the last time you were on vacation.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "What happened? Was it funny? Scary? Was it an accident?", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write a blog entry or an e-mail to a friend (8-10 lines).", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Describe the event. Remember to use the Past Continuous and Past Simple tenses.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Read your story aloud to your partner.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"content": "I write about an event that happened to me. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I describe the event.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about what I was doing when something happened.", "type": "text"}]}], "labs": [{"exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "I can talk about injuries and accidents. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can talk or report about actions, events or people.  ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "I can say what I was doing when something else happened. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": "What's the most exciting thing that happened to you on a vacation? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": "Did you ever have an accident when you were on a vacation? ", "type": "Free Header Item"}]}, {"type": "group", "contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}]}, {"content": {"allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}]}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": "Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": "The vacation was exciting! Here's what happened ...", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "img_path": "", "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "type": "STI", "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}], "selected": 0, "id": 1}], "_data": [{"type": "question", "contents": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}]}], "id": 0}], "_data": [{"type": "instructions", "contents": [{"content": "Sally tells her mother about the time she was almost in an acci